[ti:Ka Kau Question]
[ar:VESAHE · hkfaduio]
[al:Sanatan & Devotional]
[by:Radio Vaigyaaniq — draft timing, unverified]
[00:08.00]ekla chalo re... nahi...
[00:10.55]k.. ka... kaa... kaaa... kyaa...
[00:13.10]ka kau ke... ken kabhyaam kai...
[00:15.65]🎤 Narrator (Sanskrit / Nirukta 1.1):
[00:18.20]यास्कः कथयति –
[00:20.75]कः इति ब्रह्म। प्रश्नः एव सृष्टिः।
[00:25.84]🎵 Poet responds:
[00:28.39]kavim kaviim kavayah
[00:30.94]kahaam katham kathaam
[00:33.49]kasmin kyo keshu
[00:36.04]poet, to the poet, of poets
[00:38.59]where, how, what story
[00:41.14]in which? why? in the hairs…
[00:43.69]🎤 Narrator (Gurmukhi – Japji Sahib, Pauri 1):
[00:46.24]ੴ ਸਤਿ ਨਾਮੁ ਕਰਤਾ ਪੁਰਖੁ ਨਿਰਭਉ ਨਿਰਵੈਰੁ
[00:48.78]Ek aonkar sati namu karata purakhu nirabha-u niravairu
[00:53.88]🎵 Poet responds:
[00:56.43]ka kaa rahasya niraalaa
[00:58.98]kya kaun kab kaise kahan
[01:01.53]nai brahmaand racha daalaa
[01:04.08]the secret of 'ka' is strange
[01:06.63]what who when how where
[01:09.18]you just created a new universe
[01:11.73]🎤 Narrator (Devanagari – Kabir, Bijak, Ramaini 1):
[01:14.27]कंकर काहे करै तक़रीर
[01:16.82]काबा कौन, कौन बुतखाना
[01:19.37]Kankar kaahe karein taqeer
[01:21.92]Kaaba kaun, kaun but-khaana
[01:24.47](Why does a stone receive worship?
[01:27.02]What is Kaaba? What is a temple of idols?)
[01:29.57]🎵 Poet responds:
[01:32.12]khaali karo kya kahe kabeer
[01:34.67]kuttaa kaalaa kya jaane
[01:37.22]empty yourself, what does Kabir say
[01:39.76]what does a black dog know
[01:42.31]kaaba kaun, kaun but-khaana
[01:44.86]kaa de chakkar mein kaalaa phire
[01:47.41]what is Kaaba, what is the idol-house
[01:49.96]in the cycle of 'kaa', even the beloved wanders
[01:52.51]🎤 Narrator (Devanagari – Gorakhnath, Siddha Siddhanta Paddhati):
[01:55.06]नादात्मकं जगत्सर्वं
[01:57.61]नाद एव परं पदम्
[02:00.16]Nādatmakaṃ jagatsarvaṃ
[02:02.71]Nāda eva paraṃ padam
[02:05.25](The whole universe is made of sound.
[02:07.80]Sound alone is the supreme state.)
[02:10.35]🎵 Poet responds:
[02:12.90]khaak se kaaya, kaaya se kaam
[02:15.45]kaam se krodh, krodh se jaam
[02:18.00]dust to body, body to desire
[02:20.55]desire to anger, anger to death's wine
[02:23.10]kaun si kaayaa kaahe si kathaa
[02:25.65]kaa kaa rahasya – bas kaal kaa naath
[02:28.20]which body, what story
[02:30.74]the secret of 'ka' – just the Lord of Death/Time
[02:33.29]🎤 Narrator (Kannada – Allama Prabhu, Vachana 272):
[02:35.84]ಎಲ್ಲ ಕವಿಗಳು ಹೋದರು
[02:38.39]ಗುಹೇಶ್ವರನ ಲಿಂಗವ ಬಲ್ಲವರಾರು
[02:40.94]Ella kavigaḷu hōdaru
[02:43.49]Guhēśvarana liṅgava ballavarāru
[02:46.04](All poets have gone.
[02:48.59]Who knows Guheshwara’s Linga?)
[02:51.14]🎵 Poet responds:
[02:53.69]kahaam gaye sab kavim kaviim
[02:56.23]kavayah kaahe bane nayeem
[02:58.78]where have all poets gone
[03:01.33]why have the poets become so soft
[03:03.88]kasmin jag mein kyo nahi chain
[03:06.43]keshu hi to hai maaya mail
[03:08.98]in which world is there no rest
[03:11.53]it's in the hairs themselves – the filth of illusion
[03:14.08]🎤 Narrator (Gurmukhi – attributed: Chaupa Singh Rahitnama / Bachittar Natak bhava):
[03:16.63]ਕੜਾ, ਕਛੈਰਾ, ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ, ਕੰਘੀ, ਕੇਸ
[03:19.18]ਇਹ ਪੰਜ ਕਕਾਰੇ ਸਾਚੇ ਭੇਸ
[03:21.72]Kaṛā, kachaerā, kirpān, kanghī, kes
[03:24.27]Iha pañj kakāre sāce bhes
[03:26.82](Kada, kachera, kirpan, kangha, kesh –
[03:29.37]These five Ks are the true disguise.)
[03:31.92]🎵 Poet responds:
[03:34.47]e mera naanak we matwaalaa
[03:37.02]kaa de chakkar k nu dala
[03:39.57]oh my Nanak, you intoxicated one
[03:42.12]you threw me into the whirlpool of 'kaa
[03:44.67]kada kachcha karpaan kanghi kesh
[03:47.21]sakkhe purus nu ditte bhes
[03:49.76]bracelet, shorts, sword, comb, hair
[03:52.31]you gave disguise to the truest being
[03:54.86]chanddalaa de dna nai
[03:57.41]onnu wi dohkaa de daalaa
[03:59.96]not even a gift to the outcaste
[04:02.51]but you deceived even him
[04:05.06]🎤 Narrator (Panini / Sanskrit Grammarians, chanting):
[04:07.61]कः – कौ – के
[04:10.16]केन – काभ्याम् – कैः
[04:12.70]कस्मै – काभ्याम् – केभ्यः
[04:15.25]कस्मात् – काभ्याम् – केभ्यः
[04:17.80]कस्य – कयोः – केषाम्
[04:20.35]कस्मिन् – कयोः – केषु
[04:25.45]🎵 Poet responds:
[04:28.00]ka kau ke – teeno paal
[04:30.55]ken kabhyaam – dohe ka jaal
[04:33.10]ka, kau, ke – three worlds
[04:35.65]ken, kabhyaam – the net of duality
[04:38.19]kai – kaahe ko kai baar
[04:40.74]kathaam katham – kahta hai koi bichaar
[04:43.29]kai – why so many times
[04:45.84]kathaam katham – someone speaks a thought
[04:48.39]🎤 Narrator (Whispered, then loud):
[04:50.94]कः कः कः कः कः
[04:56.04]🎵 Poet (Solo):
[04:58.59]ka kaa rahasya – kya bataaye
[05:01.14]kya likhe kaghaz kya mitaaye
[05:03.68]the secret of 'ka' – how to tell
[05:06.23]what to write on paper, what to erase
[05:08.78]🎤 Narrator + Poet Together (Call and response style):
[05:11.33]Narrator asks Poet answers
[05:13.88]जेह? (jeh – which?) सो का (so ka – that 'ka')
[05:16.43]कवन? (kavan – what?) सो ख़ास (so khaas – that special one)
[05:18.98]कहाँ? (kahan – where?) सो ख़ंजर (so khanjar – that dagger)
[05:21.53]किस करण? (kis karan – for what reason?) सो किरण (so kiran – that ray)
[05:24.08]Final line – all together:
[05:26.63]so kaal – so khaas – so khanjar – so kiran
[05:29.17]that Time – that Special – that Dagger – that Ray
[05:31.72]k.. ka... kaa...
[05:34.27]kaaa...
[05:36.82]kyaa?
